nabre_text:
R/. Their message goes out through all the earth.

I - The heavens declare the glory of God; the firmament proclaims the works of his hands. Day unto day pours forth speech; night unto night whispers knowledge. There is no speech, no words; their voice is not heard; He has pitched in them a tent for the sun;

R/. Their message goes out through all the earth.

rsvce_text:
R/. The bridegroom is here;

daughters of kings are among your ladies of honor; at your right hand stands the queen in gold of Ophir. Hear, O daughter, consider, and incline your ear; forget your people and your father's house;

R/. The bridegroom is here;

the people of Tyre will sue your favor with gifts, the richest of the people with all kinds of wealth. The princess is decked in her chamber with gold-woven robes;

R/. The bridegroom is here;

in many-colored robes she is led to the king, with her virgin companions, her escort,  in her train. With joy and gladness they are led along as they enter the palace of the king.

R/. The bridegroom is here;

nabre_text:
R/. The bridegroom is here;

Daughters of kings are your lovely wives; a princess arrayed in Ophir’s gold comes to stand at your right hand. Forget your people and your father’s house,

R/. The bridegroom is here;

honor him, daughter of Tyre. Then the richest of the people will seek your favor with gifts. All glorious is the king’s daughter as she enters, her raiment threaded with gold;

R/. The bridegroom is here;

The maids of her train are presented to the king. They are led in with glad and joyous acclaim; they enter the palace of the king.

R/. The bridegroom is here;

Your arrows are sharp; peoples will cower at your feet; the king’s enemies will lose heart.

R/. The bridegroom is here;

nigeria_text:
R/. The Lord will bless his people with peace.

Ascribe to the Lord, you heavenly powers,
ascribe to the Lord the glory of his name;
bow down before the Lord, majestic in holiness.

R/. The Lord will bless his people with peace.

The voice of the Lord upon the waters,
the Lord on the immensity of waters;
the voice of the Lord full of power;
the voice of the Lord full of splendour.

R/. The Lord will bless his people with peace.

The God of glory thunders;
in his temple they all cry, “Glory!”
The Lord sat enthroned above the flood;
 the Lord sits as king forever.

R/. The Lord will bless his people with peace.

