rsvce_text:
R/. My soul is thirsting for the living God;

As a hart longs for flowing streams, so longs my soul for thee, O God. My soul thirsts for God, for the living God. When shall I come and behold the face of God?

R/. My soul is thirsting for the living God;

Oh send out thy light and thy truth;let them lead me, let them bring me to thy holy hill and to thy dwelling! Then I will go to the altar of God,to God my exceeding joy; and I will praise thee with the lyre, O God, my God.

R/. My soul is thirsting for the living God;

nabre_text:
R/. My soul is thirsting for the living God;

I - As the deer longs for streams of water, so my soul longs for you, O God. When can I enter and see the face of God?

R/. My soul is thirsting for the living God;

Send your light and your fidelity, that they may be my guide; Let them bring me to your holy mountain, to the place of your dwelling, Then I will praise you with the harp, O God, my God.

R/. My soul is thirsting for the living God;

