nigeria_text:
R/. In your strength, O Lord, the king rejoices.

In your strength, O Lord, the king rejoices;
how greatly your salvation makes him glad!
You have granted him his heart’s desire;
you have not withheld the prayer of his lips.

R/. In your strength, O Lord, the king rejoices.

You came to meet him with blessings of prosperity;
you have set on his head a crown of pure gold.
He asked you for life and this you have given:
days that will last from age to age.

R/. In your strength, O Lord, the king rejoices.

By your saving help great is his glory;
you have bestowed upon him majesty and splendour;
you have granted him blessings forever,
made him rejoice with the joy of your presence.

R/. In your strength, O Lord, the king rejoices.

rsvce_text:
R/. Here am I, Lord;

He put a new song in my mouth,a song of praise to our God.Many will see and fear, and put their trust in the LORD.

R/. Here am I, Lord;

Thou hast multiplied, O LORD my God,thy wondrous deeds and thy thoughts toward us;none can compare with thee!Were I to proclaim and tell of them, they would be more than can be numbered. Sacrifice and offering thou dost not desire;but thou hast given me an open ear.  Burnt offering and sin offering thou hast not required.

R/. Here am I, Lord;

Sacrifice and offering thou dost not desire;but thou hast given me an open ear.  Burnt offering and sin offering thou hast not required. Then I said, "Lo, I come; in the roll of the book it is written of me;

R/. Here am I, Lord;

I delight to do thy will, O my God; thy law is within my heart."

R/. Here am I, Lord;

nabre_text:
R/. Here am I, Lord;

Many shall look on in fear and they shall trust in the LORD.

R/. Here am I, Lord;

You, yes you, O LORD, my God, have done many wondrous deeds! And in your plans for us there is none to equal you. Should I wish to declare or tell them, too many are they to recount. Holocaust and sin-offering you do not request;

R/. Here am I, Lord;

Holocaust and sin-offering you do not request; so I said, “See; I come with an inscribed scroll written upon me.

R/. Here am I, Lord;

I delight to do your will, my God; your law is in my inner being!”

R/. Here am I, Lord;

