R/. The Lord is my shepherd;

rsvce_text:
R/. Blessed are the poor in spirit;

I will incline my ear to a proverb; I will solve my riddle to the music of the lyre. Why should I fear in times of trouble, when the iniquity of my persecutors surrounds me,

R/. Blessed are the poor in spirit;

men who trust in their wealth and boast of the abundance of their riches? Truly no man can ransom himself,  or give to God the price of his life, for the ransom of his life is costly, and can never suffice,

R/. Blessed are the poor in spirit;

But God will ransom my soul from the power of Sheol, for he will receive me. [Selah] Be not afraid when one becomes rich, when the glory of his house increases.

R/. Blessed are the poor in spirit;

For when he dies he will carry nothing away; his glory will not go down after him. Though, while he lives, he counts himself happy, and though a man gets praise when he does well for himself,

R/. Blessed are the poor in spirit;

nabre_text:
